---
import TokenSaving from "./TokenSaving.astro";

// One pass, one file, one Kivgraph version. Everything below is the aggregate
// of `benchmarks/graph-tools-comparison/results-all.json` -- commit `954b9eb`,
// generated 2026-08-22, question set `all`, tokenizer `o200k_base`, kivgraph
// `0.5.0`, over a corpus of 37 private git repositories.
//
// It is deliberately not a best-of. The previous version of this section paired
// a token total from one pass with an exactness score from a second and index
// times from a third, and the headline figure it printed appeared in no
// committed file at all. Quoting one pass costs a better-looking number and
// buys a number that can be checked.
const figures = [
  {
    value: "35,961",
    unit: "tokens",
    label: "Kivgraph graph queries",
    ours: true,
  },
  { value: "267,980", unit: "tokens", label: "grep + file reading" },
  { value: "28 / 29", unit: null, label: "exact answers, both arms" },
];

const provenance = [
  ["questions", "29 across six sets"],
  ["corpus", "37 git repositories"],
  ["version", "kivgraph 0.5.0"],
  ["commit", "954b9eb"],
  ["tokenizer", "o200k_base"],
];

// The counterweight is part of the evidence, not a disclaimer under it. Both
// numbers are from the same file as the figures above.
const counterweight = [
  "Precision was 1.00 on both arms. Kivgraph missed one TypeScript test file; grep missed one cross-repository consumer that never spells the symbol.",
  "The median question cost 5.95x less through the graph, with the widest margin at 86.8x. grep was cheaper on five of the twenty-nine, between 0.26x and 0.53x, and every one of those five was a question both arms answered fully.",
  "One corpus, one machine, one tokenizer. o200k_base is a proxy for the tokenizer an agent actually pays, so the ratio between the rows is the claim and the absolute values are not.",
];
---

<div class="space-y-10">
  <p class="max-w-[68ch] text-sm leading-6 text-gray-300">
    The alternative to a code graph is not being wrong. It is spending the
    context. So the benchmark's sixth arm is <code>grep</code> and reading the
    files — what an agent already does — and both arms are scored against a
    ground truth written by hand, question by question.
  </p>

  <dl
    class="grid grid-cols-[repeat(auto-fit,minmax(min(14rem,100%),1fr))] gap-10"
  >
    {
      figures.map((figure) => (
        <div>
          <dd
            class:list={[
              "font-mono text-3xl leading-none font-medium tracking-tight tabular-nums sm:text-4xl",
              figure.ours === true ? "text-graph-exact" : "text-gray-100",
            ]}
          >
            {figure.value}
          </dd>
          <dt class="mt-3 text-xs text-gray-400">
            {figure.unit !== null && <span>{figure.unit} — </span>}
            {figure.label}
          </dt>
        </div>
      ))
    }
  </dl>

  <div class="max-w-2xl">
    <TokenSaving />
  </div>

  <dl
    class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-8 gap-y-2 border-t border-rule pt-10 font-mono text-xs"
  >
    {
      provenance.map(([key, value]) => (
        <div class="flex items-baseline gap-2">
          <dt class="text-gray-400">{key}</dt>
          <dd class="text-gray-300">{value}</dd>
        </div>
      ))
    }
  </dl>

  <ol class="space-y-5">
    {
      counterweight.map((item, index) => (
        <li class="flex gap-3 border-t border-rule pt-5 text-xs text-gray-400">
          <span class="shrink-0 text-graph-exact" aria-hidden="true">
            {`0${index + 1}`}
          </span>
          <span>{item}</span>
        </li>
      ))
    }
  </ol>

  <p class="max-w-[68ch] text-xs leading-5 text-gray-400">
    The harness, the hand-written ground truth and the verbatim response of
    every call are published beside the numbers in
    <code>benchmarks/graph-tools-comparison/</code>, so any figure here can be
    checked against the bytes it came from — including the five where we lose.
    The five-way comparison against four other code graphs is a separate pass
    and is reported separately: <a
      class="text-accent-200 underline decoration-rule underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-accent-200"
      href="/comparison/">explore the benchmark</a
    >.
  </p>
</div>
